.TH \fBdraw_astg 1cad
.SH NAME
\fBdraw_astg\fR	- draw a Petri net (or a Signal Transition Graph)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdraw_astg\fR [\fIoptions\fR]* [\fIinfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBdraw_astg\fP is a tool that draws a Petri net from a description is astg
format (SIS compatible). It can generate descriptions in different formats:
PostScript, MIF (FrameMaker graphics), HPGL (HP pen plotters), PCL (Laserjet
printers, GIF (bitmap graphics) and DOT (graph format for dot).

In case the input file describes a state graph or a Petri net with only
1-token state machine, \fBdraw_astg\fP can depict a state
graph (nodes and labeled arcs).

\fBdraw_astg\fP calls \fBdot\fP, a preprocessor designed at AT&T 
for drawing directed graphs.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP 1.2i
\fB-h\fP
Help mode, prints the usage.
.TP
\fB-v\fP
Print version only.
.TP
\fB-ip\fP
Show implicit (1-fanin 1-fanout) places.
.TP
\fB-sg\fP
Depict the net as a state graph. It only works if the specification
is a state graph or a Petri net with only a 1-token state machine.
.TP
\fB-bin\fP
Depict the net as a state graph with binary encoding of the signals
and shadowed states with CSC conflicts. This option only works when
the input file has been generated with \fIwrite_sg\fP \fB-bin\fP.
.TP
\fB-bw\fP
Output a black-and-white picture. Recommended for black-and-white printers.
.TP
\fB-nonames\fP
Do not show place names and transition indices in Petri nets and do
not show state names in state graphs.
.TP
\fB-noinfo\fP
Suppress information about signals in the caption of the figure.
.TP
\fB-cn\fP
Assume the net is a Context Net (with self-loop places) and depict context 
arcs as dotted arcs.
.TP
\fB-T\fP\fIfmt\fP
Select the output graphic format. Valid values for \fIfmt\fP are
\fIps\fP (PostScript), \fImif\fP (FrameMaker graphics), \fIhpgl\fP
(HP pen plotters), \fIpcl\fP (Laserjet printers), \fIgif\fP (bitmap
graphics) and \fIdot\fP (dot format). If the \fB-T\fP option is not used,
\fBdraw_astg\fP generates PostScript format.
.TP
\fB-TB\fP
Generate a top-bottom-oriented layout (default).
.TP
\fB-LR\fP
Generate a left-right-oriented layout.
.TP
\fB-a4\fP
Generate a layout for an A4-sized sheet (default).
.TP
\fB-a3\fP
Generate a layout for an A3-sized sheet.
.TP
\fB-letter\fP
Generate a layout for a letter-sized sheet.
.TP
\fB-landscape\fP
Rotate layout 90 degrees.
.TP
\fB-nobox\fP
Show transitions with no boxes (only labels).
.TP
\fB-x[cm]\fP\fIn\fP
Define the maximum width of the layout (in cm).
.TP
\fB-y[cm]\fP\fIn\fP
Define the maximum height of the layout (in cm).
.TP
\fB-xin\fP\fIn\fP
Define the maximum width of the layout (in inches).
.TP
\fB-yin\fP\fIn\fP
Define the maximum height of the layout (in inches).
.TP
\fB-o\fP \fIoutfile\fP
Write the output to \fIoutfile\fP. Otherwise, the result
is written to \fIstdout\fP.

.SH ADVANCED OPTIONS
.TP 1.2i
\fB-nofold\fP
Do not fold layout. If this option is not specified, the layout is folded
to reduce its height. This option is suggested as an alternative way of
generating the layout to improve its planarity.

.SH EXAMPLES
\fBdraw_astg graph.g -o graph.ps\fP
.sp
generates a PostScript file for the Petri net described in \fIgraph.g\fP.
.sp
\fBdraw_astg graph.g -x10.5 -y12 | ghostview -\fP
.sp
generates a 10.5cm x 12cm layout in Postscript format. The output is
displayed through \fIghostview\fP.
.sp
\fBpetrify graph.in  | draw_astg -Tmif -o graph.mif\fP
.sp
generates a picture of the STG generated by \fBpetrify\fP in MIF format
and writes the output into the file \fIgraph.mif\fP.
.sp
\fBwrite_sg -bin graph.g | draw_astg -bin -noinfo -o graph.ps\fP
.sp
generates a state graph from the STG described in \fIgraph.g\fP and
generates a picture with information about binary codes and CSC conflicts.
Caption on signal information is suppressed.

